{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463785-apex-predator-personal-paradigm","id":1463785,"title":"Apex Predator Personal Paradigm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-13T21:08:10-07:00","id":1463785,"title":"Apex Predator Personal Paradigm","content":"Plot-wise, this has to do with misdirecting the players a little, on the subject of Jhor, where one would think the Euthanatos character more likely to have this type of Quiet than the Verbena, who is the one afflicted. I am trying to fit his Magickal Practice to his Personal Paradigm, but I am limited a little by Sphere ranks. With Prime 5, you can convert a human into Quintessence at the cost of their life. I generally don't go over rank 4 in Spheres for anyone and Prime 5 is too powerful. I'm looking at something like Prime 3, Life 4, Matter 3, Forces 3, Mind 2. He lives deep in the woods and can turn into an invisible bear. I am wondering if that combo allows him to eat biomass and convert it to Quintessence.<br /> <br /> At best, his Paradigm is about plant-predator alliances, where predators protect plants from overbred herbivores. There are some unique Magickal plants he has selectively cultivated to facilitate alchemy. He has extended the definition of herbivore to lumber company executives who would consider clearcutting in the region or even select-cutting in <i>his</i> forest. At worst, his Jhor has led him down a path toward murderous psychopathy, supported by the ideological mandate to protect nature.<br /> <br /> In terms of gaining something from killing humans, I want to explore possibilities beyond Quintessence. It might be by using Prime and Matter to create spider-silk and then trapping someone who he has lured back to his territory. With a trapped person, the luxury of time and the Sphere build above, what could you extract?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T00:41:55-07:00","id":1463803,"title":"","content":"If he's going for the kill personally, you can ditch Prime entirely in this setup, as he'll be transforming the corpse on the spot.<br /> <br /> One thing that occurred to me was the idea of &quot;returning to the cycle of life&quot;, making the mauled into special humus. In practice the character could use Life 3, Matter 2 to turn the corpse directly into new plants, adding other Spheres as needed to make them special plants.<br /> <br /> And the bits he ate... well, he ate them. He can either use magic to improve his own metabolism using them, or he can let nature do its job and use magic on his feces for similar results from above.<br /> <br /> With Mind and/or Spirit he can trap the person's soul or conscience in the new plants, as long as he doesn't let then go immediately after the kill, he can even use Entropy to bind the person's destiny or Correspondence to bind its connections. But as long as the person is killed first and the corpse used, neither Life nor Prime must be especially high, Prime isn't even needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T03:39:13-07:00","id":1463813,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> Fungal intelligence is this whole theory advanced by Paul Stamets. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mPqWstVnRjQ&amp;t=1214s\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mPqWstVnRjQ&amp;t=1214s</a><br /> <br /> I could give Paul Joyce a giant cellar that is a Sanctum for growing a necrotic fungal network. He can access it from the outside by tunneling with Matter Magick. I could have an actual dungeon like in classic D&amp;D with Monsters of some kind.<br /> <br /> Brilliant. Good suggestions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}